The seventeen 68000 binaries a standalone build contains: the sixteen
cores and the program stub.

The Maven build writes them here, as it writes them into the classes the
jar is made of, and they are committed: a Go module fetched by its import
path contains the files a commit has in it, so an executable built from
one embeds these.

BinariesTest reads them against the assembly the build makes, so one that
does not match what rmac writes today fails the build.

A tree without them does not contain one, and Read then returns an error:
doc/BINARIES.md defines each of them, and YMXR_68K names a directory to
read them from instead.
